Z||000011||bcwawright||05-16-2001||10:10 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by skitime:<BR><B>Well I will drink a cold brewsky tonight and dedicate to you anyway.  I have not heard of anyone putting 18s on a Fiero chassis but I guess it might work if you use a skinny enough tire.  How was the tracks increased that much.  Man I wish you had a camera. I would like to see that too.  You should drive that machine up to Carlisle Kit Car show this weekend.  I will be there and could check it out.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>The track is increased in the front by using Held motorSports wide track upper and lower A=arms in the front ...rear was increased using spacers but held makes a wide track rear set up but the guy I bought the car from didn't go that route because you have to lengthen the axles. Sorry I can't go to Carlisle...really want to...this is the only F355 in the country that has the F375 hesdlight system(no popup system)...if I made a mold these lights will fit regular Fieros...it would come with a new front decklid and uses Lexus SC400 double round light system(HID) with a clear lean cover plate that is flush w2ith body work..totally awesome...Have fun at Carlisle....If you get a chance could you ask around and see if anybody has or is making a F355 replica dash with center console<P>Bruce<BR>88GT Turbo F355 Spyder replica <P>||||reg||1
